{ What is the first thing you do when emerging out of the opening stage or just seeing a previously unknown puzzle? Obviously, you start off by evaluating the position, that is determining who is better depending on the entirety of elements present on the board. Based on that, a plan is usually formulated, indicating not only the suggested further course of action for yourself, but also what you should be watching out for when it goes for the rival’s intentions. Please bear in mind, however, that evaluation always comes back to us like a boomerang towards the end of our calculation process too. What would be the point of honing your calculation skills if you were unable to properly assess the positions arising afterwards? } 
1.--   

[Event "Calculate Like a Beast: The Moranda Method"]
